    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **58 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. The endpoint now flags the row instead of removing it, GET still returns it (with `deleted: true`), newly created owners are `deleted: false`, and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`, `Boolean`, defaulting to `FALSE`) with getter/setter. The default ensures freshly built owners are `false`.\n- **`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`** \u2014 replaced `repository.delete(owner)` with `owner.setDeleted(true)` + `repository.save(owner)`, so the record is retained and flagged.\n- **`rest/function/owner/CheckIdentityUnique.java`**, **`CheckHouseholdUnique.java`**, **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 each now skips any owner with `deleted == true` when scanning existing owners, so a soft-deleted owner no longer blocks a create.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema (and to its `required` list), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"deleted\", ignore = true)` to the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping so create requests keep the entity default (`false`).\n- **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the SQL schema is authoritative).\n\nI left the legacy `jdbc` repository implementation untouched \u2014 it already ignores all the newer owner columns and isn't exercised by the tests (which run under `spring-data-jpa`).",
